    "text": "It has to be something other than them voting on their own pay raises and benefits. There's no reason to pay them with federal dollars as they're not really federal employees, they're their states employees more than federal employees. Take at least some of the financial incentive to be there away.\nPersonally I say we turn all of DC into a giant museum and have a rotating Capitol, every state takes their turn having the Capitol, and we limit our \"representatives\" to only 2 weeks a quarter where they can vote on anything or even talk to each other. They've shown pretty clearly we can't trust them to run the country without some very strict rules and regulations for them to follow so it's time we give them some.",
